{{about|the game mechanic|support gem|Ballista Totem Support}}
'''Ballista totem''' is a subtype of [[totem]] skills.

Currently all gems related to ballista totem have [[totem]] and [[projectile]] [[gem tag]]s. Except {{il|Focused Ballista Support}}, all gems also have the [[bow]] tag. All 3 ballista totem active skill gems are [[attack]] skills.

Some [[passive skill]]s exclusively affect only ballista totems. Majority of passives that affect totems also affect ballista totems.

==Gems==
{{Drop enabled gem table
|where = skill.description LIKE "%Ballista%Totem%"
}}

==Passive skills==
{{Query base passive skills
|where=
  passive_skill_stats.id LIKE "%ballista_totem%"
}}

===Cluster Jewel passive skills===
The following [[Cluster Jewel]] passives are related to ballista totem:
{{Passive skill table
|q_where=
  passive_skills.id LIKE "affliction%"
  AND passive_skills.stat_text LIKE "%ballista_totem%"
|large=1
|stat_text=1
}}

===Ascendancy passive skills===
The following [[Ascendancy passive skill]]s are related to ballista totem:
{{Query ascendancy passive skills
|where=
  passive_skill_stats.id LIKE "%ballista_totem%"
}}

==Related modifiers==
The following modifiers that have spawn weight, are related to ballista totem:

===Item mods===
{{Query spawnable modifiers
|where=mod_stats.id LIKE "%ballista%totem%" AND mods.generation_type NOT IN ( "10", "31")
|stat_text=1
|spawn_weights=1
|level=1
|generation_type =1
}}

===Legacy mods===
{{modifier table
|q_tables = mod_stats
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_stats._pageID
|q_where=mod_stats.id LIKE "%ballista%totem%" AND mods.generation_type IN ( "10", "31")
|stat_text=1
|spawn_weights=1
|level=1
|generation_type =1
}}

==Unique items==
The following unique items are related to ballista totem:
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|tables=item_stats
|join=items._pageID=item_stats._pageID
|where= items.stat_text LIKE "%ballista%"
|level=1
|stat=1
|large=1
}}

==Version history==
Ballista totems used to be called '''Ranged attack totems''' or '''RAT'''.
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.11.1d|
* '''Ballista Totems''' no longer play surge effects.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.10.0|
* Fixed a bug that could cause '''Ballista Totems''' to magically float. Flying isn't planned until Path of Exile 6.
* All [[totem]]s and '''ballistas''' now have approximately 50% more base [[life]] than previously, with the exception of [[Ancestral Protector|Ancestral Totems]], [[Decoy Totem]]s and [[Holy Flame Totem]]s, which had higher base life already. These totems have received a smaller increase to their base life.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.9.0|
* Ranged attack totems are now called Ballistas and have a cool new look. It's a Ballista!
* Artillery Ballista now has a 30% damage penalty against players.
* All Ballista Totem skills (such as {{il|Siege Ballista}} and Ranged Attack Totem, which has been renamed Ballista Totem) now place the totem at Melee range.
* Added a new Dexterity Skill Gem - {{il|Artillery Ballista}}: Summons a Ballista Totem that propels a sequence of fiery arrows into the air. The arrows impact the ground in a line, each dealing area damage to the enemies around it.
* Added a new Dexterity Skill Gem - {{il|Shrapnel Ballista}}: Summons a Ballista Totem that fires multiple arrows with extreme force, breaking them apart into shrapnel. Enemies can be hit by multiple arrows from the same attack.
* Ranged Attack Totem Support (Now called {{il|Ballista Totem Support}})
** Supported skills now deal 50% less Damage at gem level 1 (from 30%), up to 41% less at gem level 20 (from 26%).
** Supported skills now summon a Ballista Totem, rather than a regular Totem.
** Supported skills now have +2 to maximum number of Summoned Ballista Totems.
** Attacks used by totem now have 50% less Attack Speed at all gem levels (from 30% less).
* Siege Ballista's gem text now states that the skill summon a ballista totem rather a regular totem. {{Undocumented}}
}}
{{Version history table row|2.4.1|
* Most totem skin microtransactions can now be applied to all types of totems (other than Ancestral totem).
}}
{{Version history table row|2.1.0|
* {{il|Siege Ballista}} is introduced to the game. (Note: At that time does NOT specify as its own Ballista category)
}}
{{Version history table row|0.10.2|
* Added a new cosmetic microtransaction effect - {{il|Tiki Totem Skin|Tiki Totem}}: Replaces the standard [[Spell Totem]] or Ranged Attack Totem with a coloured totem that has carved tiki designs.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.12m|
* Introduced to the game as support skill {{il|Ballista Totem Support|Ranged Attack Totem Support}}.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

